From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:36:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: initialise the HTC TX works before a start can
 fail

ath10k_htc_wait_target() initialises bundle_tx_work and
tx_complete_work only once the target has answered. When it fails, for
example because the firmware never sends the HTC ready message,
ath10k_core_start() unwinds through ath10k_htt_tx_free() and
ath10k_htc_stop_hl(), which calls cancel_work_sync() on the work items
that were never initialised:

  WARNING: kernel/workqueue.c:4409 at __flush_work+0x334/0x358
  Call trace:
   __flush_work+0x334/0x358
   cancel_work_sync+0x6c/0x90
   ath10k_htc_stop_hl+0x20/0x64 [ath10k_core]
   ath10k_htt_tx_free+0x20/0x5c [ath10k_core]
   ath10k_core_start+0x3cc/0x10f0 [ath10k_core]
   ath10k_core_register_work+0x590/0x96c [ath10k_core]

On WCN3990 this happens when the modem, which manages the WLAN firmware,
is stopped while the first firmware start is waiting for the target.

Initialise the works in ath10k_htc_init(), which every start runs before
anything can queue or cancel them.

Fixes: c8334512f3dd ("ath10k: add htt TX bundle for sdio")

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htc.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htc.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htc.c
index 821a12090b..01d896520b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htc.c
@@ -995,9 +995,6 @@ int ath10k_htc_wait_target(struct ath10k_htc *htc)
 			   htc->alt_data_credit_size);
 	}
 
-	INIT_WORK(&ar->bundle_tx_work, ath10k_htc_bundle_tx_work);
-	INIT_WORK(&ar->tx_complete_work, ath10k_htc_tx_complete_work);
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -1296,6 +1293,8 @@ int ath10k_htc_init(struct ath10k *ar)
 	struct ath10k_htc_svc_conn_resp conn_resp;
 
 	spin_lock_init(&htc->tx_lock);
+	INIT_WORK(&ar->bundle_tx_work, ath10k_htc_bundle_tx_work);
+	INIT_WORK(&ar->tx_complete_work, ath10k_htc_tx_complete_work);
 
 	ath10k_htc_reset_endpoint_states(htc);
 
